WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.190
H-Hey... Doesn't this mean...

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.750
Seriously?

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.060
Look. The end of the rope...

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:10.110
If it's over there, that means...

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.030
<b>Rabbit Tasting</b>

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.240
it's... still alive... right?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:27.710
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.510
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.470
I...

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.390
I'm... going to try to do it!

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.070
A-Are you sure?

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.410
I'm gonna pull it.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.990
There might really be a rabbit there!

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.700
Y...

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.620
Yes!

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:47.410
<i>A rabbit!</i>

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.870
<i>We really caught one!</i>

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.290
This is crazy...

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.640
This is crazy! Crazy! Crazy!

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.170
Let's go get Homare!

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.810
W-We can't!

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.080
It might get away...

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.660
We have to do it ourselves!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.130
Why... Why won't you die?

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.830
You're not athletic. Quit trying so hard.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.850
I can't handle the idea
of killing animals either...

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.330
But...

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.600
I can't watch you cry, Mutsu.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.210
There wasn't a rabbit in the trap.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:04.110
No. We ended up wasting energy.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:04.920
Yeah...

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.740
Hey!

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.080
We got one!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.550
Good work. Both of you.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.860
I'm so shaky I feel like I'm about to collapse.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.720
If Asuka-san hadn't been there,
it would have gotten away.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.390
One head of rabbit.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.530
This will provide us quite a lot of food.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.330
We can grill it, and if there's
any left, we can dry the meat.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.360
You don't use "head" to count rabbits...

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.150
First we'll make a knife for breaking it down.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.020
W-We're starting there?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.820
When animals die, their
organs decompose quickly,

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.450
so we have to retrieve them quickly.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.330
At this temperature, the meat will
go bad in about an hour, but...

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.500
in this water temperature,
it should last a little longer.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.750
Good. There's no way we're wasting that meat.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.320
So what are we going to do about a knife?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.800
We'll make a stone knife.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.680
<b>Stone?</b>

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:04.890
Stone?

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.680
<b>Stone?</b>

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.710
Stone?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.680
<b>Stone?</b>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.680
Stone?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.490
You tap rocks together like this and pick
the stone that makes the highest noise.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.620
When you hit the edges like this

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.810
it chips like a seashell, you see?

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.100
Carefully, a little at a time...

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.110
<i>I wonder if I have a knack for this.</i>

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.250
Irritated

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.300
Tap
Tap

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.380
Tap
Tap

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.170
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.270
<i>Everyone's so focused it's hard to say anything...</i>

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.720
That'll do it.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.510
Now, to get to work.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.430
Um! Homare-san!

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.960
I... want to try breaking down the carcass!

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.600
I was useless when we had to kill it!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.270
Are you serious, Mutsu?

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.420
I see.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.750
Rabbits are mammals, but breaking
them down is fairly simple.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.940
You should try it.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.990
O-Okay!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.330
So... I should cut here?

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.900
Mutsu. If you put the blade in
like that, you'll cut into the organs

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.560
and ruin the meat.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.730
Pinch and pull, and try to cut just that part.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.130
O-Okay!

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.720
Hey, now. Are you all right?

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.670
Next, put the blade inside
and face it outwards.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.430
Cut towards the tail.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.560
That's right.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.250
Just like that.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.880
Remove the organs.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.610
I... I-I...

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.570
I did it...

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.160
Next, you have to skin it, but...

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:53.970
Should I take over?

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:56.830
No! Please let me do the whole thing!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.410
I think I'm starting to get used to it...

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.280
and I'm learning a lot!

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.250
I see. Then, let's continue.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.200
Next, we'll remove the head and feet.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.250
We can't cut through bone, 
so feel for the joints and cut there.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.330
Okay!

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.680
I...

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.650
I did it!

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.540
That's amazing! It really looks like meat!

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.360
It... It really does.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.210
So how do we cook it?
Just grill the whole thing?

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.430
Good question.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:35.030
When I went to the south of France
on a family vacation, I had lièvre!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.680
First, the chef came to the table
and showed us the rabbit

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.500
saying, "I will be preparing this."

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.100
Of course, he used every part of the rabbit

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.000
making soup from the bones...

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.720
There were even courses that
used the blood and marrow.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.550
Couldn't we do something like that?

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.390
I don't think so.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:58.280
First, we should probably cut it up soon.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.980
With the meat we can make lièvre à la vapeur.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.850
We can make soupe de lièvre.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.590
Today we'll have French cuisine for dinner!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.910
Now, everyone. Let's get ready.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.000
S'il vous plait!

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.820
All of a sudden she's giving orders...

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.700
Let's see. For ingredients we have rabbit meat...

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.490
salt made from seawater...

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.910
and leopard plant stems.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.500
Hey, teacher! I don't think we have
enough ingredients or equipment!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.000
No complaints!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.340
You can do it if you put your mind to it!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:29.890
First, vapeur... that is, 
we'll steam the meat, but...

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:34.630
In that case, I know a method
I read in a UK special forces manual.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.760
That doesn't sound reassuring...

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.770
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:39.160
I see!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.350
First, cut the meat along
the backbone and break it in half.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.650
Cut off the front and back legs...

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.440
then debone all the pieces.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.030
Oh, it's all messy...

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.950
It is lacking in elegance, isn't it?

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.130
This is my first time with
French food and rabbit meat!

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.340
Plus, all I have to work with is a stone knife!

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.250
I'm sorry! It just slipped out...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.830
Mucchan, you're scary.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.840
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.840
Leopard Plant

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.840
Leaves
 Roast over a fire and massage
 to release juices.
 Use for bruises, cuts, swelling, etc.
 Stems
 Edible once astringency is removed
 Use in tsukudani, soup, pickles, etc.
 Roots
 Dry and store
 Use for upset stomachs, diarrhea, 
food poisoning, etc.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:08.320
I see.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.870
First, dig a pit.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.790
Line it with hot rocks.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.320
Cover it with sand.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.360
Lay out some leaves.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.520
Wrap the rabbit meat in leopard
plant leaves and place them inside.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.020
Lay more leaves on top and
cover with more rocks.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.750
We'll light a fire on top of the rocks.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.950
It should take about 50 to 60 minutes.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.660
But how will we keep track of the time?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.460
Huh?

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.530
Once the shadow has moved 15 degrees
away from this rock, it's been an hour.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.720
<i>A kitchen timer?</i>

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.000
<i>Who'd have expected a sundial?</i>

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:51.640
Then, while we're waiting, we can make soup.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.880
We use heat to get stock from the bones...

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.350
Use salt for the seasoning, and...

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.690
Were there any other ingredients?

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:00.920
When I had it, there was zucchini in it.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.060
Do you think we have any zucchini?

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.410
These leopard plant stems.
Do you think we could add them?

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.840
Let's try it!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.110
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.110
Really?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.000
It's probably about ready.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.200
I wonder if it worked.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.710
I'll try opening one.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.240
Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:19.950
It's hot!

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.080
It doesn't seem burned...

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.510
It smells delicious! I think it worked!

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.190
Let's lay out the soup and eat it over here!

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:35.630
At first I thought Shion-san's
idea was impossible,

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.180
but it looks like it might work out!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.110
French food in a place like this.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:41.370
None of the rest of us would've thought of it!

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.310
It looks super yummy!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.250
Right? I said we could do it
if we put our minds to it!

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.900
Thank you for the food!

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:52.820
It's so good!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.240
Soup from the south of France!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.660
It tastes like mizutaki!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.250
It's soup from southern France.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.780
Oh, uh... right.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.510
But, you know, this broth is really nice.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.830
Yes! It's light and delicious!

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.080
Homare, would it be okay 
to eat the meat now...

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.650
You're already eating it!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.450
Huh?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.410
Hey. What's rabbit like? What's it taste like?

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:13.050
Huh?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.570
It... tastes like rabbit...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.780
Fine! I'll just try it myself!

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.060
<i>So good!</i>

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:26.370
<i>It's like chicken! It's so tender!</i>

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.450
<i>It's so juicy! Delicious!</i>

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.100
<i>We love meat!</i>

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:38.050
<i>It's delicious!</i>

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:40.090
<i>Meat is the best!</i>

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.990
That was so good...

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:49.800
We ended up eating all of it,
so we couldn't preserve any.

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.460
Well, we were all hungry, so...

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:58.090
This is the first time since
coming to this island that I'm full.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.810
Thank you. It was delicious.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:29.280
Next time, Case 7:
 "Exploring the Island."

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.010
<b>Exploring the Island</b>
